  "full_text": "So I just took a shower in this, or a shower. Anyway, that was a trip. Like, I didn't fucking do this, right? It was too hard to strip down. My boxers walked in, got wet. Put on soap, swum in, and dried off, right? Damn, it's faster than anything. Anyway, so fucking, man, wham, bam. And then, like, I had to walk with dirty feet. Then I put water in there. I just put a pot and then like washed off my feet. And then bam. Pretty damn fast. See Mr. God says. Mr. God says. Holy sheep shit. Never fucking thought I'd be doing this. Worry is worthless. My soul takes refuge in you. In the shadow of your wings I will take refuge until destruction passes by. Worry is a complete waste of energy. Soul is nothing. That's why Jesus said. Which of you by being anxious can add a cubit to his lifespan. In essence, he says, you go to bed tonight, fret and fuss because you're not five foot 11, you're only five foot nine. When you wake up in the morning, you're still gonna be five foot nine. Worry will never make you stretch. It won't solve your anxiety in your mind either. Then maybe you'll be completely again. It's not for me. I don't know where he's been. Preaching to the choir. Okay, so when it gets cold, I don't know where. I'm gonna be I'm just taking it day by day I won't maybe I won't be here so",
